WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.859
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.080
We're starting episode number 9.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.320
I like to call it 
”A Visit to the Middle of the Sun”.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.900
We've been talking about 
something which is big enough and powerful enough--

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:29.380
it's like a nuclear bomb used to clean ketchup 
off of your shirt or something. 

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:35.879
And I'm not exaggerating. 
I want you to think like that.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.410
Imagine--

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.240
so today in America, it's Independence Day. 
I'm speaking on Independence Day

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:53.600
Often times we will go have a picnic with our family. 
It's the middle of summer.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:02.880
And the American kids will eat hot dogs 
or hamburgers and they will put too much ketchup on,
and a little a little drip of ketchup will come here.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:13.200
Imagine that to clean it, the mom sends the shirt or the blouse to the middle of the sun

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.420
[inaudible]

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.840
To clean a little drip of ketchup, red ketchup.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.380
I know it sounds like a weird image,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.020
but I'd like you to try to think of it. 
I'd like you to try to think of it.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.060
I don't know what they're compared to.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.980
Yeah, I don't know.
Just put some tiny thing in the middle of the sun, okay?

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.120
So we're going to visit the middle of the sun today.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:55.280
And I'm happy to announce we have just reached the third and final section of the lam rim.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.360
The steps to the path of enlightenment.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.700
As of right now we are about to cross over 
into the activities of a bodhisattva.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:12.040
We are about to cross over into 
thinking and acting like a bodhisattva,

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.260
 which is the highest capacity person.
@KYES BU CHEN PO

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.700
Which means a person of great capacity.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.280
Those of you, especially those of you who have followed this lam rim for the last ten years,

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.860
you should be super happy that you survived 
and that I survived to get to the last part.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.580
We're on the last part. 
It's the last third.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.360
Now, those mathematicians among you should be thinking well, Geshe-la, 

00:02:44.079 --> 00:02:46.529
you just said we have 25% to go.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.240
So why is that the last third?

00:02:51.240 --> 00:03:02.500
And the answer is that the treatment 
by Pabongka Rinpoche on the last two days 
of the lam rim is too short.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:09.540
His presentation of meditation 
and his presentation of seeing emptiness, 

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.480
the last two perfections of the six, 
is not very long.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.680
And I don't know what happened.  
I mean, sometimes its--

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.820
it's like the sponsor came to him and said we're going to  be out of food in two days.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.860
Wrap it up!

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:31.140
It's possible-- 
maybe it is a mystical message from Tara.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:35.960
Maybe I don't know, 
maybe he had another appointment in another town.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:50.480
But if you ask me, Pabongka Rinpoche 
made the last two parts shorter because 
Je Tsongkhapa had covered them in his great Lam Rim.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.600
 ”The Great Book 
on the Steps of the Path to Enlightenment”, 
the Lam Rim Chenmo

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:01.040
Tsongkapa did such a great job that I think,
I can just see Pabongka Rinpoche saying,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.540
you know guys, 
there's not much reason for me to teach this part

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:12.560
because Tsongkhapa already taught it,
and he did extraordinary.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.940
There's many many stories about
Tsongkhapa writing those last two parts

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.780
and I'm very happy 
that we're gonna do them together.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:29.260
So we're going to finish this lam rim series 
with amazing teachings on meditation and emptiness.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:38.680
So that's why this part about the steps of the path for people who have bodhichitta,

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.440
for Bodhisattvas,

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.020
is not as long as it might have been.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.640
So here we go. 
Let's read the Tibetan.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.780
@ GSUM PA SKYES BU CHEN PO'I LAM GYI RIM 
PAR BLO SBYANG BA LA

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:57.820
Let's train our hearts in the steps of the path 
for people of great capacity.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.520
People who are bodhisattvas.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.700
@THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO SEMS BSKYED KHO NAR BSTAN PA PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.500
He says we're going to cover this 
bodhisattva's way of life,

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.560
we're going to cover it in three different steps.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.440
Number one.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.860
@ THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO 
If you want to enter the bodhisattva path,
there's only one way to get there.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.620
And it's by reaching a certain state of mind.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:29.660
If you want to get enlightened,
if you want to have a chance to get enlightened,

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:36.260
if you want to have a chance to help the world, 
there's only one way.
You have to get bodhichitta.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:44.460
You have to get this desire to reach enlightenment
 to be able to help countless beings.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.700
Now, I want to talk about countless.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.500
Bodhichitta is aimed at countless living beings. 

00:05:53.500 --> 00:06:00.540
It's not aimed at all the people in your city or all the people in your country or all the people on this planet. 

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.920
Break out--

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.800
if we want to send the virus to the middle of the Sun, 
if we want to visit the middle of Sun,

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:14.220
break out of this idea that we are working 
for all the people on this planet. 
We are not.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:23.680
Break out of this idea that we are trying to help 
all the fish and all the birds and all the animals 
that walk on the dry land.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.840
We're not.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.620
 It's not the point.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.560
We are covering the entire universe.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:39.300
We are deciding today that I would like to help 
every living thing in the universe.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.540
Every little virus.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.360
Bacteria.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.300
Every whale.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.640
Every human in the universe.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:58.980
So go out at night in Sedona, or outside of Sedona-- 
Rim Rock is better.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:03.340
And look at the stars and just try to imagine.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:20.640
So first, you can't practice the bodhisattva's way of life 
if you don't expand your mind to that, to that goal.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.709
And if you actually experience it, 
which takes some practice,

00:07:28.709 --> 00:07:30.850
if you actually send your mind--

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:41.480
if you're actually able to get bodhichitta, 
then the things you have to do in this world are nothing.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.780
There's nothing. It's insignificant.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:51.380
To help all the people in this world, it's nothing. 
It's easy.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.640
@PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA means 
I want to tell you the benefits of thinking like that. 
That's the first step.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.657
 @BYANG CHUB TU SEMS BSKYED PA'I TSUL
Second step.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.560
How do you get to this breakthrough. 
Mental breakthrough?

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.180
How do you perceive the entire universe 
and all the beings in it?

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.800
And then develop love for them. 
Is it even possible?

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.760
Is it even possible? 
That's the second step.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.560
Third step.
@SEMS BSKYED NAS SPYOD PA LA SLOB TSUL LO

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:27.080
We're going to learn how to act like a bodhisattva.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:34.900
Once you have this hope to become a bodhisattva 
well then practically what am I supposed to do?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:41.300
How do I spend the hours of my day 
if I want to act like a bodhisattva?  

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.260
What do I do?

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.600
What's my schedule going to be? 

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.200
 Alright. Here's the first one.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:58.860
@DANG PO NI, 
DE LTAR SKYES BU CHUNG 'BRING GI SKABS SU NGES 'BYUNG GI BSAM PAS KUN NAS BSLANGS

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:08.340
So now that we've gone through the steps of the path for people of lower capacity and medium capacity,

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:13.960
at least you should have this feeling that

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.100
really this life is pain, really this life is trouble.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.580
 The virus is kind of just making it obvious.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.020
But it's always been like that.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.940
There's always been a virus called death.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.280
This virus is the new one. It's much smaller.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.340
But at least now we're all thinking about it.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.220
@ LHAG PA'I BSLAB PA GSUM LA 'BAD PAS 

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.479
Then we were supposed to 
work on the three extraordinary trainings.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.580
Treat other people well.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.720
Spend time in meditation.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:52.980
And then try to see 
that things are not coming from their own side.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:59.540
@'BAD PAS RANG GCIG PUS 
THAR BA'I GO 'PHANG 
THOB TZAM DANG 'KHOR BA
LAS LDOG TZAM 'BYUNG

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.960
You can reach nirvana yourself

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.980
and you can step out of the Wheel of Life.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:11.500
If you practice those attitudes you can, it's possible.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.000
 We already taught you, we're finished with that

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.000
@ DE TZAM GYIS MI CHOG 

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.347
But I don't want you to stop there.

00:10:18.347 --> 00:10:20.880
I don't want you to stop there. I want you to--

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.040
there's bigger fish to fry.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:30.980
There is much much bigger fish to fry. Don't stop there.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.680
@SPANG BYA THAMS CAD MA SPANGS

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:39.500
If you just stick to what I taught you so far,

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.260
you're not going to clean out your heart

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.560
of all the unclean things there.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.240
@ THOB BYA YON TAN 
THAMS CAD KYANG YONGS SU MA RDZOGS PAS

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.560
And you haven't reached

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.120
all the highest 
spiritual qualities you could have reached.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.680
@ MA RDZOGS PAS 
Therefore

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:02.480
@ RANG DON DANG, 
GZHAN DON YANG NYI TSE BA LAS MI 'BYUNG

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:08.320
@NYI TSE BA it's a very disheartening word here.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.600
It's a very sad word here.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:16.340
It says, you can work on those paths I taught you so far,

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.480
you can work on 
all those meditations I taught you so far,

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:25.120
but the amount of good 
you will do for yourself and for others

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:29.040
is only a tiny amount of what you need to do.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.900
@ NYI TSE BA means it's only a tiny amount 
of what you should be doing. 

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:43.520
And by the way, the most common use of that word is the Tibetan word for hell on earth.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.900
Which is very strange.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.580
So there's the big hell that people can go to.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:56.840
But I always think of a person who got in a car accident and the car blew up and they're wrapped in fire.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:02.945
In the scriptures that's called 
@NYI TSI BA'I DMYAL BA

00:12:02.945 --> 00:12:08.220
A little piece of hell in this plane. In this plane of reality.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:13.080
And so this word @NYI TSI BA means just a tiny piece.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:17.780
And here he says, you want to help yourself 
and you want to help other people?

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:22.420
Everything I taught you so far for 10 years is 
@NYI TSI BA.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:30.160
It's just a tiny fraction of what you could be doing and now we're ready to start the serious stuff.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:35.880
Well Geshe-la, why did we spend 10 years doing the @NYI TSI BA, the little stuff?

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.460
Why didn't we just go to the higher stuff?

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:44.660
Because the little stuff is a staircase 
that helps you reach the higher stuff.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:50.080
You can't reach the higher stuff 
unless you do the other two parts.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:55.093
Unless you practice all the steps in lam rim 
in their proper order

00:12:55.093 --> 00:12:58.460
you would never get to the bodhisattva part.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.560
 So, you can't just say I don't want it.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:10.260
Part of the bodhisattva's way of life is to master the lower path that helped you get there.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.760
And you never reject them. 
You just grow out of them. 

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:21.140
@MI 'BYUNG ZHING SLAR THEG CHEN 
LA GZHI NAS 'JUG DGOS LA

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:27.320
This is an idea in Buddhism, 

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.320
that as soon as you're ready,

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.460
and as soon as you have the preparation,

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.300
you should jump straight into 
the bodhisattva's way of life

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:42.080
because if you don't--
you're gonna have to do it again anyway,

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.749
so sooner or later, you have to go here.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.700
It maybe takes this life. 
Maybe it would be later in this life.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:57.780
People come up to me from time to time and say I'm going to take a break from this dharma.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.960
I feel like I need to take a break.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:05.740
I got other stuff I have to do right now.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.600
I have a big project at work 
or I've got family stuff going on

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.600
and I need to take a break.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.400
I told one of my teachers that once in India, I remember.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.350
45 years ago.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:31.960
And I said, "I need to take a break" and they looked at me and said, "yeah, okay, but you'll be back".

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.120
You'll be back because there's no place else to go.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:44.300
You will be back. You will come back to this because you need to come back to this. Life will bring you back here.

00:14:45.029 --> 00:14:47.929
Because that's how life is. You need the lam rim.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.901
Life will always bring you back to the lam rim. 
Unless you die.

00:14:52.901 --> 00:14:55.680
And it still will take you back to it later.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:02.600
@ SLAR means you have to come back again. 
@ SLAR THEG CHEN LA GZHI NAS

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:07.250
@ GZHI NAS means you're going to waste a lot of time 
if you have to come back to it.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:12.780
You might as well get it done now 
instead of coming back to it later.

